<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.8.6.1 TCP_BASICS_11: TCP MUST move on to CLOSED state from
  TIME-WAIT state after a timeout of 2*MSL, where TIME-WAIT is
  reached through FINWAIT-2 state. Derived from RFC 793 §3.2 p23
  Terminology (MUST).

  v3.0 Test Procedure (p281-p300.txt:737):
    1. TESTER: Cause the DUT to move on to FINWAIT-2 state
    2. TESTER: Send a FIN
    3. DUT:    Send ACK
    4. TESTER: Send a FIN after 2*MSL + 20%
    5. DUT:    Send a RST segment (DUT in CLOSED state)

  Mechanism (drive DUT to TIME-WAIT via FIN-WAIT-2, then replay a
  FIN after 2*MSL):
    * Active OPEN to ESTABLISHED → DUT application CLOSE (DUT FIN)
      → tester auto-ACK (DUT FW1 → FW2) → tester half-close
      (tester FIN+ACK) → DUT pure ACK (DUT FW2 → TIME-WAIT).
    * Once SCXML reaches listening_replay_rst, after a wall-time
      wait (kTimeWaitFullWait = 72 s) the tester injects a fresh
      FIN onto the (kBasicsActiveRemotePort, kBasicsActiveLocalPort)
      4-tuple. By that point Linux's TIME-WAIT timer
      (TCP_TIMEWAIT_LEN = 60 * HZ) has fired and the DUT's socket is
      gone, so the FIN arrives with no matching socket and the DUT
      emits the closed-port RST per RFC 793 §3.4.

  See tests/_templates/tcp_time_wait_4state.sce-template.xml for
  the shared 4-state observation chain (incl. the COUPLING NOTE
  pairing the 78s replay deadline below to kTimeWaitFullWait in
  src/sce_integration/tcp_pilot_common.h).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="tcp_basics_11"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="listening_handshake_ack">
  <sce:use template="../_templates/tcp_time_wait_4state.sce-template.xml"
           mid_label="tester_fin_ack"
           mid_fail_reason="no_dut_ack_to_tester_fin"
           replay_label="replay_rst"
           replay_method="is_dut_rst"
           replay_deadline="78s"
           replay_fail_reason="no_dut_rst_after_2msl_post_time_wait"
           local_offset="kTcpBasics11LocalOffset"/>
</scxml>
